LEVELS = []
def L(number,title,meta,mission,route,lock,twist,enemies,recovery,secret):
    LEVELS.append(dict(number=number,title=title,meta=meta,mission=mission,route=route,lock=lock,twist=twist,enemies=enemies,recovery=recovery,secret=secret))
L(1,'The Broken Footbridge','2–3 min   Difficulty 1   Gentle horizontal route',
'Reach the ranger hut and relight the trail marker.',
'Begin on continuous ground, climb a broad stump, then cross a short visible gap. A lower trail loops back to the stump so a missed tutorial jump is recoverable.',
'A fallen branch hides the receiver. Push the marked branch aside with the context action, then illuminate the receiver for 1.2 seconds to latch the bridge.',
'The bridge extends away from the player, exposing a small alcove underneath. The alcove is optional and returns to the main trail.',
'No damaging enemies. One harmless moth circles a lantern to preview light attraction.',
'Shrine before the bridge. Falling onto the lower trail costs no heart; falling beyond it returns to the shrine with the bridge state retained.',
'A firefly behind the stump teaches checking below a route.')
L(2,'The Acorn Courier','3–4 min   Difficulty 1   Fork and reunion',
'Recover the ranger’s acorn key and open the hollow tree door.',
'The door is visible from the entrance. Upper branches lead to the key; the lower path offers a safe return and reconnects directly to the door.',
'The acorn key fits the leaf-shaped socket. Picking it up adds a persistent quest flag. Using the door consumes the key and saves the unlocked door together.',
'The key branch bends down after pickup, becoming a return ramp rather than making the player repeat the ascent.',
'One moss crawler patrols the upper branch. Its turn points leave a clear place to jump over it.',
'Shrine at the fork. A fall while carrying the key retains it; the return branch cannot strand the player.',
'A narrow lower tunnel hides a journal page and rejoins the door.')
L(3,'The Bellroot Shaft','3–4 min   Difficulty 2   Vertical climb',
'Raise a root elevator to the canopy exit.',
'Climb alternating ledges around a central shaft. Each side has a landing shelf, and a ladder shortcut opens from the highest shelf.',
'Two pressure roots must stay depressed together. Push one stone onto the lower root, then stand on the upper root to lift and permanently latch the elevator.',
'The stone used as a weight also becomes a step for reaching a side ledge; either use is reversible until the elevator latches.',
'Two crawlers on separate wide ledges. Neither patrol crosses the pressure-root interaction area.',
'Shrine at mid-height. Fallen stones respawn at their marked sockets; the latched elevator and top ladder remain open.',
'A canopy nest holds the fifth firefly above the exit shelf.')
L(4,'The Mothkeeper Garden','3–4 min   Difficulty 2   Circular courtyard',
'Free a gardener trapped behind a thorn shutter.',
'Enter a ring-shaped garden with a central cage and two side shelters. A raised rim lets the player survey both light posts before descending.',
'Light the far decoy post to draw two moths away, then cross in darkness and activate a protected lever. The lever retracts the shutter permanently.',
'Leaving the lantern on while crossing attracts the moths back. Shelter leaves provide safe places to switch light and observe their route.',
'Two lantern moths, both visible before the first crossing. A lit decoy retains their attention until the player approaches its attraction radius.',
'Shrine beside the first shelter. The decoy may be relit without limit, and the rescue flag persists after the lever is used.',
'The rescued gardener points to a seed alcove on the upper rim.')
L(5,'The Hollow Tree Observatory','4–5 min   Difficulty 2   Three room hub',
'Build a beam path that opens the observatory roof.',
'A central room connects to left, upper and right balconies. Shortcuts return each balcony to the center, allowing the player to inspect the whole circuit.',
'Rotate two mirrors through four fixed positions using context action. The correct path is lantern to mirror A to mirror B to the roof receiver; etched arrows show the required turns.',
'A decorative mirror reflects light but reaches no receiver. Its different frame and an uninterrupted view of the real roof cable make the distinction readable.',
'Two crawlers on approach ledges and one moth near the optional balcony. The mirror floor itself is safe.',
'Shrine in the hub. Mirror orientations persist there, and a reset pedestal restores only this puzzle’s mirrors.',
'A side reflection opens a cosmetic cache without resetting the roof circuit.')
L(6,'The Sleeping Root Sentinel','4–5 min   Difficulty 3   Stealth corridor with bypass',
'Carry a brass key through a sentinel’s hall to the old mill.',
'The main hall contains three stone shelters. An overhead route bypasses the last shelter but demands a longer jump; both paths reach the same door.',
'The key is on a pedestal behind the sentinel. Light wakes its scan, so turn the lantern off, wait for the head to face away, collect the key, light the receiver from the final shelter, and use the key on the mill door.',
'The exit’s receiver cannot be lit safely from the open hall. A final shelter has a slit that allows illumination without entering the sentinel’s scan.',
'One root sentinel and two crawlers in separate approach rooms. The sentinel flashes its eye before its scan begins.',
'Shrine before the hall; key ownership survives failure. The sentinel always resets to its announced starting pose.',
'The overhead bypass contains a journal page explaining the sentinel’s damaged eye.')
L(7,'The Falling Orchard','4–5 min   Difficulty 3   Descent and return loop',
'Collect two gear teeth and repair the orchard lift.',
'Descend a spiral of broad branches around a broken lift. The first descent opens a trunk ladder, making the return short and clearly visible.',
'One gear tooth rests on a branch and the other sits behind a weighted shutter. Use an acorn crate on a plate, collect the part, and install both at the lift console.',
'Marked brittle branches collapse after a two-second creak. They reveal safe lower shelves rather than dropping the player directly into an unseen hazard.',
'Two moths in the lower orchard and one crawler on a stable shelf. No enemy occupies a collapsing landing.',
'Shrine at the bottom console. Gear teeth persist when collected, and required brittle routes are replaced by the opened ladder.',
'A stable side branch leads to a hidden rescue cocoon.')
L(8,'The Two Sides of the Mill','4–6 min   Difficulty 3   Mirrored rooms with different rules',
'Restore the mill wheel and unlock its floodgate.',
'A central wheel room connects a bright upper room and a dark lower room. The player can inspect both mechanisms from the central balcony.',
'Use the upper room’s mirror to charge a latch, then lure a moth onto the lower room’s light cage so its weight holds the second plate. Both flags release the wheel brake.',
'The rooms look similar, but one needs a directed beam and the other needs a creature’s weight. Distinct beam and footprint symbols state the difference.',
'One puzzle moth and three crawlers distributed across the approaches. The moth returns to a safe perch if it loses the lure.',
'Shrine in the wheel room. Charged latch persists; the moth can always be recalled by relighting the cage.',
'A restored wheel platform reaches a loft containing an optional firefly cluster.')
L(9,'The Lockworks Under the Lake','5–6 min   Difficulty 4   Branching lock chamber',
'Open the three-ring travel lock that leads to the Beacon Stag.',
'A dry lakebed hub branches to a gear room, a symbol gallery and a receiver balcony. Each branch opens a one-way shortcut back to the hub.',
'Recover a gear to power the rings. Read leaf, moon and sun symbols in the gallery, set the rings in that order, then illuminate the exposed receiver to latch the travel door.',
'Water begins entering after the gear is installed. The rise is capped below all essential interaction points, opening a floating shortcut instead of imposing an unseen timer.',
'Two sentinels and two crawlers, separated by doors so no more than two enemies threaten a puzzle room.',
'Shrine in the hub saves gear installation and ring positions. A wrong combination resets only the rings and never consumes the gear.',
'The new floating shortcut reaches an inscription about the reversed river.')
L(10,'The Beacon Stag','6–8 min   Difficulty 4   Three phase guardian arena',
'Free the forest beacon and earn the River Seal.',
'A broad arena has three sheltered receiver stations and a central tree. Activating each station changes the safe route around the tree.',
'Phase one lights a stationary receiver. Phase two redirects a mirror during the stag’s rest. Phase three lures its charge into a marked root brace, exposing the last receiver.',
'The final charge breaks the apparent exit wall and reveals a river dock. Cracks, river sound and a view through the wall foreshadow the new route.',
'One Beacon Stag plus up to two moths in phase three. Its paw scrape and ground line telegraph every charge; puzzle progress replaces combat damage.',
'Shrine before the arena; each completed phase is saved. Retry restores three hearts and restarts only the current phase, including its safe opening.',
'An optional high perch after victory holds the forest memory and all missed arena fireflies.')
L(11,'The River That Runs Backward','3–4 min   Difficulty 2   Raft route with bank stops',
'Reach the ferry village and discover why its river reversed.',
'The ferryman grants the passive Water Ward before the first deep pool. Board a broad raft, steer left and right through gentle current lanes, and stop at two safe banks.',
'Turn a bank valve to open the village sluice. Its connecting pipe is visible from the landing, and the raft waits in a sheltered eddy while the player disembarks.',
'The shortest visible current flows away from the village. Floating leaves reveal direction; the slower outer lane leads forward and reconnects to the raft.',
'One crawler on the first bank. Deep water is safe with the ward; no aquatic enemy appears during the swimming lesson.',
'Shrine before boarding. A lost raft returns to the last dock; jumping in water strokes upward, while releasing jump lets the player sink slowly.',
'A quiet side eddy conceals a ferry token and returns to the main current.')
L(12,'The Floating Storehouse','4–5 min   Difficulty 2   Two tier flooded warehouse',
'Lift a floating crate to a high pressure plate and open the cargo door.',
'Explore a dry catwalk and a shallow lower floor. Water rises only to marked lines, carrying the crate between the two routes.',
'Unhook the crate with context action, flood to the middle mark, guide it under the plate shelf, then raise the water to the top mark. The crate’s weight latches the door.',
'The crate blocks the obvious swimming tunnel when raised in the wrong place. A drain handle reachable from every state lets the player reposition it.',
'Two reed skimmers patrol visible surface lanes. Their ripples appear before a short leap; the catwalk offers a safe observation point.',
'Shrine at the water controls. Crate position and water step are saved together; a reset handle returns both to the dry starting state.',
'A crate riding detour reaches a roof rescue cocoon.')
L(13,'The Three Waterlines','4–6 min   Difficulty 3   Vertical reservoir hub',
'Collect a tide key from the reservoir tower and unlock the upper outlet.',
'A central reservoir links three galleries at low, middle and high water. Each gallery’s icon appears beside the main valve, showing which route its level exposes.',
'Low water exposes a gear, middle water floats a lift to the key gallery, and high water reaches the outlet. Install the gear before setting the other two heights.',
'The upper key gallery looks reachable by a maximum jump, but a grille blocks it until the middle-water lift aligns. The grille cable leads visibly to the valve.',
'Two skimmers below and one crawler in the dry gallery. Only one surface lane overlaps the lift approach.',
'Shrine at the central valve saves gear and key. Every water height leaves a ladder back to the valve, preventing a sealed dead end.',
'A low-water tunnel contains a mural and returns through a ladder shaft.')
L(14,'The Mirror Pool','4–5 min   Difficulty 3   Reflection chamber',
'Use the pool surface to illuminate a receiver on the ceiling.',
'Enter on a high balcony, inspect a beam path painted on the wall, then descend to a water-height dial and two broad standing stones.',
'Set the pool to its middle mark so the beam reflects upward from the marked still-water tile. Close a small inlet to remove ripples, then hold the lantern toward that tile.',
'An active inlet makes the reflection wobble and miss. Ripple icons and the moving beam endpoint explain why a correct water height alone is insufficient.',
'Two shelled crabs guard the approach stones. Light makes them retreat into shells, allowing a safe jump past; shells are never required to hold the pool still.',
'Shrine before the dial. Height and inlet state persist, and the reflection latches once the ceiling receiver charges.',
'A second still tile reflects into a side alcove containing a cosmetic shell.')
L(15,'The Ferry Without a Ferryman','4–6 min   Difficulty 3   Branching moving route',
'Repair an abandoned ferry and choose a route through reed islands.',
'Install a nearby rudder, board the ferry, then choose between a sheltered island route and a faster current channel at a clearly marked junction.',
'Two dock switches must be pulled in either order to open the final bridge. Each switch creates a return eddy so choosing one branch cannot lock out the other.',
'The apparently fast channel loops to the start until its dock switch reverses the current. Signposts and a visible returning raft make the loop understandable.',
'Two skimmers in the channel and one crab on the sheltered dock. Enemy placement gives each route a different problem rather than a simple difficulty label.',
'Shrines on both main docks save switch flags. Falling overboard returns the player to a boarding ladder, and the ferry waits at the nearest dock.',
'An optional third island holds a passenger’s journal.')
L(16,'The Eel Lantern Tunnel','4–6 min   Difficulty 4   Underwater stealth descent',
'Carry a glow pearl through a submerged tunnel to a sealed air chamber.',
'Descend through wide pools separated by stone cover. Ceiling pockets show the next opening, and bright exit markings remain visible with the lantern off.',
'The pearl is a quest item that powers the chamber door. Light attracts current eels, so switch off to pass their nests and use safe recesses to inspect the route.',
'The pearl’s soft glow is harmless to eels; only the player’s bright lantern draws them. A first eel demonstrates this safely behind a grille.',
'Three current eels and one crab, separated into distinct pools. Eels display a charged stripe before lunging and cannot enter marked recesses.',
'Shrine before the deep pool retains the pearl. The Water Ward removes oxygen pressure; failure restarts the local pool, not the whole descent.',
'A side current carries the player to an abandoned diver’s shelter.')
L(17,'The Twin Cisterns','5–6 min   Difficulty 4   Connected tank puzzle',
'Balance two cisterns to raise a pair of counterweighted doors.',
'A dry bridge overlooks left and right tanks. A center transfer valve moves one marked unit of water between them, while two supply valves set the initial total.',
'Use the etched target marks: left tank at two units and right tank at one. Put the floating weight in the left tank, then close both supply valves to stabilize the doors.',
'Matching the visible waterlines is insufficient while a supply valve is open. Animated gauge needles and dripping pipes show the instability.',
'Two crabs on outer platforms and two skimmers in tank lanes. The center valve deck remains safe for planning.',
'Shrine on the bridge. Water quantities, weight socket and valve states save as one snapshot; an accessible drain restores the initial quantities.',
'A stable high tank uncovers a room behind a waterfall.')
L(18,'The Breathing Floodgate','4–6 min   Difficulty 4   Timed passage with refuge rooms',
'Open an old gate whose pressure doors alternate between wet and dry.',
'Three short chambers cycle water on a visible gauge. Each has a raised refuge and a window showing the next door before entry.',
'Cross while the gauge is below the blue notch, then pull a refuge lever that permanently disables the completed chamber’s cycle. Repeat for the next chamber.',
'The final chamber reverses the door’s timing, but an open-door symbol on its gauge and a safe demonstration cycle announce the change before commitment.',
'Two eels and two skimmers, with only one active threat in a timed chamber. None can enter a refuge.',
'Shrine between chambers two and three. Mistiming floats the player back to the refuge; cycling water alone never causes instant death.',
'An optional slower refuge route contains the fifth firefly.')
L(19,'The Sunken Archive','5–7 min   Difficulty 4   Exploration hub with changing access',
'Find three tide inscriptions and set the archive’s exit lock.',
'The archive has a main reading hall and three galleries reached at different water heights. Opening a gallery creates a permanent ladder or swimming shortcut.',
'Collect the wave, reed and shell inscriptions. Their wall positions show bottom to top order; set matching symbols on the exit rings and illuminate the door seal.',
'One gallery entrance floods after its inscription is taken. A newly floating shelf leads back to the hall, teaching the player to read changed terrain.',
'Two crabs, two eels and one skimmer across separate galleries. The reading hall contains no enemies.',
'Shrine in the hall saves inscriptions and water state. Gallery clues are copied into the pause journal, so returning for a forgotten symbol is unnecessary.',
'A drained reading pit reveals a traveler’s account of the fire mountain.')
L(20,'The Tide Warden','6–8 min   Difficulty 5   Guardian arena with water levels',
'Restore the river’s direction and earn the Ember Seal.',
'Three valve platforms surround a central basin. The guardian circles the basin, while ladder shafts keep every valve reachable at each approved water height.',
'Phase one lowers water to expose a seal. Phase two uses a floating crate to hold a valve plate. Phase three redirects the warden into a breakable grate, then lights the final seal.',
'After the second seal, the current reverses. A warning bell, leaf movement and a safe pause announce the reversal before the guardian resumes.',
'One Tide Warden; two skimmers enter only in phase three. A widening ripple marks its sweep, and raised islands remain safe during each attack.',
'Shrine before entry; completed phases persist. Retry restores the current phase’s crate, water level and guardian position together.',
'After victory, freely explore the drained basin for missed collectibles.')
L(21,'The First Ember','3–4 min   Difficulty 3   Safe volcanic foothills',
'Obtain the Ember Lens and open the mountain road.',
'Begin on cool rock with a view of lava below. A forge keeper gives the lens, then demonstrates a brazier from behind a protective wall.',
'Hold the lit lantern toward the marked brazier for 1.2 seconds to ignite it. Its heat lowers a metal road barrier; the metal barrier cannot be burned directly.',
'Nearby red flowers resemble fuel but are decorative. Only the brazier carries a flame socket, making valid heat targets recognizable.',
'One cinder hopper beyond the tutorial barrier. It crouches and glows before jumping; broad cool ledges provide landing room.',
'Shrine at the lens station. Falling into lava returns to the shrine with the lens retained; the tutorial brazier stays lit.',
'A cooled side ledge leads to the forge keeper’s first journal.')
L(22,'The Furnace Lungs','4–5 min   Difficulty 3   Alternating vent corridor',
'Reach the furnace bellows and shut down the crossing vents.',
'Move through three vent lanes with heatproof alcoves between them. The camera shows a complete active and inactive cycle before the first required crossing.',
'Close two fuel valves in either order. Each permanently stops its vent lane; a final bellows handle opens the exit once both valves are closed.',
'One vent stays dark before firing, but the pressure gauge still climbs. Gauge movement and a hiss carry the same warning as the other vents’ glow.',
'Two cinder hoppers on cool islands and one ash wasp over an optional cache. Required waiting alcoves contain no enemies.',
'Shrine before the second valve. Closed valves persist; an interrupted cycle restarts with a full warning and an inactive first beat.',
'A deactivated vent shaft reveals an optional descent and return ladder.')
L(23,'The Charred Vine Stair','4–6 min   Difficulty 3   Vertical route transformed by heat',
'Clear the watchtower stair without destroying its only support.',
'Ascend a ruined stair with marked dry vines, green structural roots and a movable stone brace. Preview the broken upper landing through an open wall.',
'Push the brace into its marked socket before igniting the dry vine bundle. The brace catches the falling stair section and forms a climbable slope to the door lever.',
'Burning the bundle first drops the stair into a safe lower channel. A winch returns it, allowing the player to add the brace and try again.',
'Two hoppers and one wasp, each on a separate tier. Fire events pause nearby patrols briefly so the transformation remains readable.',
'Shrine at the brace socket. The winch is reachable in both stair states; a successful brace and stair configuration persists.',
'A green root path leads to a nest with the fifth firefly.')
L(24,'The Ash Wasp Foundry','4–6 min   Difficulty 4   Suspended catwalk loop',
'Recover an insulated key from the upper foundry and open its service lift.',
'A loop of suspended catwalks surrounds three heat sources. Safe roof pockets connect to a central lift shaft and provide a route back after pickup.',
'Ash wasps avoid strong heat. Ignite decoy braziers to shift their patrol lanes, collect the insulated key, then use the service lift door below.',
'Lighting all braziers at once crowds the wasps onto the key route. Numbered vent diagrams suggest lighting only the outer two; braziers can be extinguished at their valves.',
'Three ash wasps and one hopper. Their flight lanes update visibly before the player leaves a safe pocket.',
'Shrine by the lift saves the key and brazier settings. Wasps return to defined perches on retry; the key cannot be dropped into lava.',
'A deliberately dark inner lane opens access to a maintenance cache.')
L(25,'The Cooling Garden','4–6 min   Difficulty 3   Water and heat combination hub',
'Create a stable stone crossing over a lava channel.',
'A safe garden hub connects a water pipe room and a furnace valve room. A balcony overlooks the crossing and displays its stone-forming sockets.',
'Close the furnace feed, align the water spout, then release one measured water burst. Cooling forms temporary stones; closing the feed first makes them permanent.',
'Cooling while the feed is open produces cracked stones that reheat after a clearly shown countdown. The spout can refill without consuming a collectible.',
'Two crabs near the pipe and two hoppers near the furnace. Each branch uses its own familiar enemy behavior.',
'Shrine in the garden. Water supply is unlimited, stone sockets are deterministic, and a reset valve drains a failed crossing safely.',
'A spare cooled stone reaches an abandoned greenhouse.')
L(26,'The Forge Guard Bargain','5–6 min   Difficulty 4   Enemy used as a mechanism',
'Use a guard’s hammer strike to break the chain sealing the forge.',
'Enter a broad workshop with two pillars, a marked chain anchor and a sheltered receiver. A balcony allows observation of the guard’s patrol.',
'Activate a light decoy at the chain anchor. Hide behind a pillar while the forge guard winds up its hammer; the strike breaks the anchor, exposing a receiver that opens the door.',
'The guard ignores an unlit decoy. A practice strike against a marked scrap plate demonstrates the sound and impact radius before the required lure.',
'One forge guard, two hoppers and one wasp across the workshop approaches. The guard cannot strike through a shelter pillar.',
'Shrine before the workshop. Broken chain persists; a missed strike resets the decoy after a short cooldown with no limited resource.',
'A second optional anchor opens a smith’s tool cabinet.')
L(27,'The Glass Rail Escape','4–6 min   Difficulty 4   Moving carriage with station puzzles',
'Carry a prism across a cooling rail and unlock the upper station.',
'Ride a slow cargo carriage between three safe stations. Each station has room to leave the carriage, inspect the next track and operate a switch.',
'At the first stop, align a track. At the second, cool a missing rail socket. At the third, install the prism to power the station lock; the carriage waits until recalled.',
'The central track splits around a collapsing arch. Warning cracks and a visible alternate rail appear before departure, so the route choice happens from a safe platform.',
'Two wasps near outer track sections and two hoppers at separate stations. No required interaction occurs on a moving carriage.',
'Shrine at every station saves prism ownership and completed repairs. The carriage respawns at the latest station after a fall.',
'The longer rail branch stops at a hidden overlook.')
L(28,'The Smoke Library','5–7 min   Difficulty 4   Puzzle rooms with controlled visibility',
'Recover the furnace code and open the sealed lift.',
'Three compact library rooms connect through a clear central hall. Opening shutters removes smoke from one room at a time, revealing shelves and floor markings.',
'Use visible vent handles to clear each room, collect three embossed code plaques, then match their shapes to the lift’s rings. Plaques remain readable in the journal.',
'The final plaque is reflected in polished metal. A small normal-orientation example beside it teaches reading the reversed inscription.',
'One forge guard and two wasps, separated by shutters. Enemies cannot attack from smoke outside the player’s current visible room.',
'Shrine in the clear hall. Plaques persist; closing one shutter always opens its return vent so the player cannot be sealed inside smoke.',
'A fully cleared side shelf contains the furnace keeper’s memory.')
L(29,'The Heart Before the Fire','5–7 min   Difficulty 5   Preparation hub with optional order',
'Disable three furnace feeds before entering the mountain heart.',
'A triangular hub joins a vent tower, cooling channel and guarded workshop. Each branch ends with a shortcut back to the center.',
'The tower valve stops pressure, the channel valve cools a bridge, and the workshop lever releases the heart door chain. Complete them in any order; three visible pipes report progress.',
'Each disabled feed changes the hub: lower steam, a new stone platform or an opened ladder. These changes shorten the remaining branches rather than adding surprise hazards.',
'Two guards, two hoppers and two wasps across distinct rooms. At most three can threaten the player in one encounter.',
'Shrine in the hub saves each completed feed. Key objects return to reachable sockets if displaced; no branch requires an item consumed in another.',
'A newly cooled hub platform reaches a final optional upgrade cache.')
L(30,'The Furnace Heart','6–8 min   Difficulty 5   Guardian mechanism in a rotating arena',
'Cool the corrupted furnace and earn the Sky Seal.',
'Three stationary refuge platforms surround a rotating ring of marked stone slabs. The player observes ring direction before every phase begins.',
'Phase one shuts a fuel valve between pulses. Phase two reflects a beam to release a water tank. Phase three cools the exposed core, then lights its restoration seal.',
'The ring reverses only after a loud brake and a full safe pause. A fixed refuge stays reachable, so the reversal tests route planning rather than reflex alone.',
'One Furnace Heart mechanism and two hoppers in phase three. Vents announce attacks with a gauge, glow and sound; guardian completion requires three puzzle states.',
'Shrine before entry saves completed phases. Retry resets the current ring position, water tank and pulse cycle consistently.',
'After cooling, walk through the dormant core to collect missed rewards safely.')
L(31,'The Windglass Crossing','3–4 min   Difficulty 3   Glide lesson over recovery shelves',
'Obtain a leaf glider and reach the highland observatory.',
'A sky traveler fits the glider before a broad practice gap. Hold jump after the ascent to glide through a steady updraft; lower shelves lead back to the takeoff point.',
'A wind vane must face the observatory to release its sail door. Use context action to turn the vane, then glide along the wind ribbon that appears.',
'The strongest updraft leads to an optional high route. The required route uses a gentler current, shown by a separate trail of leaves.',
'One crawler on the arrival shelf. No airborne enemy appears during the first glide lesson.',
'Shrine at takeoff. Missed glides land on recovery shelves; releasing jump folds the glider, and another press can reopen it after a short cooldown.',
'The stronger updraft reaches a sky traveler’s journal and returns to the observatory.')
L(32,'The Anchored Windmill','4–5 min   Difficulty 3   Wind corridor with movable shelters',
'Carry an anchor block to the windmill’s locking plate.',
'Three terraces sit across a gust corridor. Heavy blocks slide only while pushed through context action and provide cover on their downwind side.',
'Push the marked anchor block along a recessed track to hold the mill plate. Then climb the sheltered stair and release the brake lever to open the door.',
'A light crate can hold the plate briefly but blows off during the next gust. Weight symbols on both objects and a safe first gust show why the anchor block is needed.',
'Two frost stalkers on separate terraces. Their tracks reveal hiding places, and they crouch before sliding out of the snow.',
'Shrine before the track. Lost blocks respawn at sockets; the plate recess keeps a correctly placed anchor from moving on its own.',
'A shelter detour leads behind the windmill to a rescue cocoon.')
L(33,'The Ice Road Below','4–6 min   Difficulty 3   Sliding descent with recovery ramps',
'Deliver a bell clapper to the valley gate.',
'Descend three ice slopes with dry landing islands and generous braking zones. A visible lower path reconnects to each island after an overshoot.',
'Take the clapper from a side workshop and install it in the gate bell. Ringing the repaired bell retracts the valley barrier.',
'The fast center slope passes the workshop. Wood signs point to a slower side ramp, while a return lift allows recovery after missing the turn.',
'Two stalkers and one wind kite. The kite’s landing shadow previews its dive, and no dive targets the first practice slope.',
'Shrine at the workshop retains the clapper. Ice acceleration is gradual; dry islands restore normal braking before mandatory interactions.',
'An optional upper slope reaches a frozen campsite.')
L(34,'The Kitekeeper Spires','5–6 min   Difficulty 4   Vertical glide and perch route',
'Light two spire beacons to open the summit elevator.',
'Climb a chain of wide perches using alternating updrafts. Each perch has a sheltered rest area and a view of the next takeoff and landing.',
'Turn each spire’s wind shutter toward a marked direction, then illuminate its beacon. The two beacon flags latch the summit elevator.',
'The second beacon’s wind must be redirected after landing. A return perch stays accessible so changing it cannot remove the only way back.',
'Three wind kites with nonoverlapping dive zones and one stalker on a side perch. Kites always show a moving shadow before diving.',
'Shrine at each spire. Beacons persist, and a missed glide resets only to the latest perch; the camera shows a kite’s entire approach.',
'A deliberate lower glide reaches a hanging garden before returning by updraft.')
L(35,'The Frozen Causeway','4–6 min   Difficulty 4   Temporary ice construction',
'Obtain the Frost Chime and make a route across meltwater.',
'At a sheltered lens station, switch the lantern to Frost. Practice freezing a marked shallow pool, then cross two pools with permanent stone rests between them.',
'Illuminate a marked water socket for 1.2 seconds to form a 12-second ice platform. Freeze the nearer socket, reach the stone rest, then freeze the far socket to reach a door lever.',
'The platform timer pauses while the player stands on it. A cracking animation and sound warn during the final three seconds of the 12-second timer, avoiding punishment during observation.',
'Two stalkers on dry banks and one kite above an optional pool. Enemies never break a required ice platform.',
'Shrine at the stone rest. Freeze sockets can be reactivated without cost, and every melted route leaves a reachable return ladder.',
'A third freeze socket opens a small ice grotto.')
L(36,'The Hall of False Stars','5–6 min   Difficulty 4   Observation puzzle with decoys',
'Identify the real star circuit and unlock the observatory vault.',
'A safe entry gallery overlooks three star pedestals. Each leads to a short testing balcony and then returns to the central floor.',
'The real circuit casts a matching shadow on the ceiling dial. Align that pedestal’s beam with the dial, then use the vault lever after the receiver latches.',
'Mirror wisps imitate fireflies near false pedestals. They lack the rescue halo and reveal a cracked silhouette in the lantern beam; the first false pedestal triggers only a harmless chime.',
'Two mirror wisps and two stalkers in separate side galleries. Wisps display their cracked silhouette before a damaging approach.',
'Shrine at the entry dial. Incorrect tests reset only the local light, and the player can inspect the real clue again without fighting.',
'A fully lit side mural identifies a route behind the star dial.')
L(37,'The Stormbound Train','5–7 min   Difficulty 4   Moving convoy with safe stations',
'Reconnect three supply wagons and carry their lantern core to the storm station.',
'The train moves slowly between sheltered stops. Cross wagon roofs during steady wind and drop inside marked hatches when a gust warning sounds.',
'At each stop, use a coupling lever after aligning its wind vane. All three couplings release the core compartment; install the core in the final station door.',
'The third wagon appears detached, but a visible lower maintenance rail carries it beneath the train. A station lift provides access without a blind jump.',
'Two kites above separate wagons and two wisps inside optional cargo rooms. Stops and coupling levers are enemy-free.',
'Shrine at every station saves coupling and core flags. Missing the train respawns it at the last stop; collected core ownership is retained.',
'A cargo roof detour reveals a passenger’s final travel note.')
L(38,'The Four Seasons Vault','5–7 min   Difficulty 5   Element station puzzle hub',
'Combine the three journey seals to open the storm vault.',
'A central lens station connects a flooded room, frozen stair and wind tower. Each room returns through a shortcut to the central door.',
'Use Water Ward to reach a submerged switch, Ember to thaw a marked stair latch, and Frost to create a stepping platform beneath the wind vane. Their three flags release the vault rings.',
'Thawing the marked latch also drains the nearby pool. The clue diagram shows this interaction; the water-room switch remains reachable by its opened ladder afterward.',
'One eel, one forge guard and two kites, each contained in its own room. Lens changes happen only at the safe station.',
'Shrine at the station saves every completed room and lens choice. Any local object reset leaves the room’s permanent shortcut open.',
'Completing the rooms in a clue-marked alternate order reveals a cosmetic vault.')
L(39,'The Beacon Road Home','5–7 min   Difficulty 5   Return journey through transformed places',
'Link the forest, river and mountain beacons before the final climb.',
'Travel through three short districts with distinct silhouettes: a restored tree bridge, a river ferry and a cooled forge. Each has a new route opened by earlier chapter victories.',
'Repair one visible cable break in each district: anchor a root lift, raise a ferry receiver with water, and cool a forge socket. Three cable lights power the summit gate.',
'The familiar forest exit is now below the trail. A repaired lift and returning gardener direct the player downward, rewarding recognition without requiring memory of the old map.',
'Two moths, one crab, one guard and one kite in separated districts. Familiar counters return with one environmental complication per room.',
'Shrine at every district boundary saves cable flags. Failure never repeats a completed district, and old shortcuts remain available.',
'A rescued traveler in each district contributes a final optional memory fragment.')
L(40,'The Stormkeeper and the Last Light','7–9 min   Difficulty 5   Final guardian with safe lens stations',
'Restore the great beacon and bring the rescued travelers home.',
'Three broad arena terraces surround the beacon. Each terrace has a sheltered lens station, a clear guardian view and a shortcut to the next completed phase.',
'Phase one diverts water to ground the storm circuit. Phase two uses Ember to free a frozen mirror and light a seal. Phase three freezes stepping stones, glides to the final receiver and restores the beacon.',
'The guardian’s apparent weak point is a decoy with a broken cable. The live cable glows toward the true receiver, repeating the observation lesson from level 36.',
'One Stormkeeper with up to two wisps in the final phase. Separate wind, sweep and lightning tells never overlap into an unavoidable landing trap.',
'Shrine before entry; each restoration phase persists. Retry returns the needed lens, water and platform states to that phase’s safe opening.',
'After victory, a free exploration state allows missed collectibles; the closing scene reflects rescued travelers without blocking the ending.')
assert len(LEVELS) == 40 and [x['number'] for x in LEVELS] == list(range(1,41))
